From 2e479209331975fca9d1f4217160cc5e1fe10e17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bert Outtier <outtierbert@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:19:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(network_adapter): report a host disconnect right away

On ESP32-C3 with ESP-IDF v6.1, a CMD_DISCONNECT from the host (for
example wpa_cli disconnect, or wpa_supplicant exiting) deauthenticates
with esp_wifi_deauthenticate_internal(). The station goes to init, but
the Wi-Fi library posts WIFI_EVENT_STA_DISCONNECTED only when the next
connection attempt ends, so the DISCONNECT_EVENT reaches the host
seconds later. Meanwhile cfg80211 still considers the station connected,
the host drops the late event for an unexpected generation, and the
station loops on auth timeouts until the driver is reloaded.

Use esp_wifi_disconnect() instead: it posts the event right away. The
deauthentication frame then carries reason 8 (leaving) instead of the
host's reason.
---
 esp/esp_driver/network_adapter/main/cmd.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/esp/esp_driver/network_adapter/main/cmd.c b/esp/esp_driver/network_adapter/main/cmd.c
index 1ed8f9e..a2d4dfd 100644
--- a/esp/esp_driver/network_adapter/main/cmd.c
+++ b/esp/esp_driver/network_adapter/main/cmd.c
@@ -2314,7 +2314,17 @@ int process_disconnect(uint8_t if_type, uint8_t *payload, uint16_t payload_len)
             s_assoc_control_port = 0;
             s_assoc_is_reassoc = 0;
             association_ongoing = 0;
-            esp_wifi_deauthenticate_internal(reason);
+            /*
+             * esp_wifi_deauthenticate_internal() takes the station to init,
+             * but then the Wi-Fi library only posts WIFI_EVENT_STA_DISCONNECTED
+             * when the next connection attempt ends. The host waits for that
+             * event to finish the disconnect, and when it finally comes it
+             * also resets the state of the new attempt. esp_wifi_disconnect()
+             * posts the event right away (the deauthentication frame carries
+             * reason 8, leaving, instead of the host's reason).
+             */
+            (void)reason;
+            esp_wifi_disconnect();
             status = CMD_RESPONSE_SUCCESS;
         }
     } else if (if_type == ESP_AP_IF) {
-- 
2.53.0

